Z||000000||wkayl||10-20-2000||01:03 PM||||Well, it was when this picture was taken on June 8, 1986.  The company I worked for gave this car away.  It was a 1986GT without a/c (like the one FieroDave has) but with an automatic.  About 10 people "found" cans of Coca-Cola with $100 printed in the bottom of the can.  They all got together and picked keys out of a fish bowl.  The 1st person (a little old lady) to try her key started the car right up.  She was from the town of 6000 people where this picture was taken during our new warehouse grand opening.  I have heard that the car is still there in a garage with less than 5000 miles on it.  I thought I had better pictures but this is the only one I found.  It may be large, but I wanted you to at least see that it is a Fiero.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grandopening_2.jpg">  <P>When I saw the one my brother's mother-in-law had 2 years ago I had to have it.  read my story about it on FieroDaves web site.  <A HREF="http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/wayne.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/wayne.html</A> <BR>or see pictures of my car on my web site.  <A HREF="http://wkayl.homestead.com/kaylfamily.html" TARGET=_blank>http://wkayl.homestead.com/kaylfamily.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
